INPUT: n, finite sets S, T ⊂ ℤ_{≥0}
1. IF S ∩ T ≠ ∅: REJECT (trivial covering by 0)
2. FOR i = 1..n: IF no (s,t) with i | s − t: RETURN 'not a covering'
3. n′ ← ⌊n/2⌋; M ← max(S ∪ T)
4. X ← ∏_{s∈S,t∈T} |s − t|          // X ≠ 0, X ≤ M^{|S||T|}
5. CHECK C(2n′,n′) | X               // Kummer: p^{v_p} ≤ 2n′
6. CHECK 4^{n′} ≤ (2n′+1)·M^{|S||T|}
OUTPUT: covering status and wall certificate

